---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Manifesto & Core Values — The Green Screen"
  description="The Green Screen explores how the places we inhabit shape our lives, and how we might reshape them in response to a changing climate."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 space-y-16">
    <!-- Brand Statement Header -->
    <header class="border-b border-blueprint pb-8 space-y-4">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-forest font-semibold block">
        BRAND POSITIONING & MANIFESTO
      </span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-forest font-semibold leading-tight">
        "Every wall has witnessed something. Every room has held a life."
      </h1>
      <p class="font-serif italic text-xl text-ink-light leading-relaxed">
        The Green Screen is a magazine of stories, essays, poetry, and ideas about the built environment, and the complicated relationship between the places we love and the futures we must build.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Mission & Vision -->
    <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-paper p-6 space-y-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-terracotta font-semibold block">MISSION STATEMENT</span>
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-forest font-semibold">Reshaping What Shapes Us</h3>
        <p class="font-serif text-sm text-ink-light leading-relaxed">
          To explore how the places we inhabit shape our lives, and how we might reshape them in response to a changing climate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-paper p-6 space-y-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gold font-semibold block">VISION STATEMENT</span>
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-forest font-semibold">Imagined by Everyone</h3>
        <p class="font-serif text-sm text-ink-light leading-relaxed">
          A world in which the future of our buildings is imagined by everyone whose life unfolds within them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Core Values Broadsheet Grid -->
    <section class="space-y-6">
      <div class="border-b border-blueprint pb-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink font-semibold">Core Editorial Values</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 font-sans text-xs">
        <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-card p-5 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-display text-base text-forest font-semibold">Intellectual Honesty</h4>
          <p class="font-serif text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            We do not simplify a question to make its answer more appealing. We acknowledge uncertainty, challenge assumptions, and let complexity remain where it matters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-card p-5 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-display text-base text-forest font-semibold">Human Empathy</h4>
          <p class="font-serif text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            Buildings are lived in before they are analysed. We attend to the memories, dependencies, inequalities, and attachments that make places meaningful.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-card p-5 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-display text-base text-forest font-semibold">Scientific Rigour</h4>
          <p class="font-serif text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            Our research is traceable, our claims proportionate to the evidence, and our technical explanations clear enough to be questioned and understood.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-card p-5 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-display text-base text-forest font-semibold">Accessibility & Inclusion</h4>
          <p class="font-serif text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            The conversation belongs to everyone affected by the built environment, not only those with the credentials or resources to shape it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-card p-5 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-display text-base text-forest font-semibold">Creative Freedom</h4>
          <p class="font-serif text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            We make room for different genres, perspectives, forms, and interpretations. No single narrative can contain the experience of a place.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-blueprint bg-canvas-card p-5 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-display text-base text-forest font-semibold">Aesthetic Integrity</h4>
          <p class="font-serif text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            Form is part of meaning. We treat words, images, data, and design with equal care, pursuing beauty without allowing it to obscure truth.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial Protocol Note -->
    <section id="methodology" class="border-t-2 border-forest pt-8 space-y-4">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-forest font-semibold block">
        EDITORIAL GOVERNANCE & PRIVACY
      </span>
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink font-semibold">How We Handle Research & Submissions</h3>
      <p class="font-serif text-sm text-ink-light leading-relaxed">
        Submissions are received through our confidential editorial intake channels. To protect contributor privacy and unpublished creative material, works under review or in revision are never stored in public repositories. Every published piece undergoes rigorous verification by retrofit engineers and architectural fact-checkers before public release.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
